        "faq1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I have to give up coffee?",
            "answer": "<p>No. MUTO is not a caffeine replacement and there is no reason to quit anything to take it. The distinction matters for a different reason: caffeine redistributes the energy you already have, and MUTO works on how much you produce. Most people find they reach for the second and third cup less often, which is a consequence rather than a rule.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "So why don’t I feel anything on day one?",
            "answer": "<p>Because anything with an immediate lift would be doing the borrowing trick. There are no stimulants in the formula deliberately. Most people describe the afternoon dip going in weeks three to four, and wearable data typically moves between day 30 and day 60.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is this the same as an energy drink with B vitamins?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Energy drinks pair a stimulant with vitamins that support energy metabolism, and the stimulant is what you feel. MUTO has no stimulant at all - the B vitamins are there in active forms because NAD⁺ production and use depend on them, not to dress up a caffeine hit.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What will I actually see on my wearable?",
            "answer": "<p>Sleep quality is usually first, because a borrowed-energy pattern shows up there most clearly. HRV and resting heart rate follow, typically between day 30 and day 60. Read all of them as weekly trends - a single morning tells you about last night, not about the product.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if my data doesn’t move?",
            "answer": "<p>Then you send it back. The 90-day money-back guarantee exists because the honest test is your own numbers rather than how the marketing reads. Log your 30-day HRV, resting heart rate and sleep averages before you start so the comparison means something.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        }
